1
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:12,800
Hi, Michelle.

2
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,830
Hello, Harry.

3
00:00:13,830 --> 00:00:15,410
It's nice to see you again.

4
00:00:15,410 --> 00:00:16,480
Hello.

5
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:18,190
Hi, Susan.

6
00:00:18,190 --> 00:00:20,550
We have both been excited about seeing you

7
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:22,530
and having lunch with you today.

8
00:00:22,530 --> 00:00:24,540
Michelle picked these flowers out for you.

9
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:27,990
Daddy, can we go soon?

10
00:00:27,990 --> 00:00:30,330
We're going to go to lunch in a few minutes, honey.

11
00:00:30,330 --> 00:00:32,740
But I'm thirsty.

12
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:37,570
OK. You go out and get a drink of water at the fountain.

13
00:00:37,570 --> 00:00:39,200
The fountain is over there, Michelle.

14
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,620
Near the Exit sign.

15
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:48,480
Thank you.

16
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:51,230
Michelle is a little shy.

17
00:00:51,230 --> 00:00:54,760
I used to be that way when I was her age.

18
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:57,540
Harry, if Michelle doesn't want to go,

19
00:00:57,540 --> 00:00:59,030
we don't have to.

20
00:00:59,030 --> 00:01:00,150
She'll be fine.

21
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:00,780
Remember,

22
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:04,060
I haven't dated any one else since her mother died.

23
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:06,650
This is a little difficult for her.

24
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:07,720
Are you ready to go?

25
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:10,820
Yes. But could you wait one minute?

26
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:12,600
I have a call to make.

27
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:18,950
Would you excuse me?

28
00:01:18,950 --> 00:01:21,600
Sam, get Mr. Levine at Toytown Stores

29
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:23,060
on the telephone for me, please.

30
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:29,990
Right.

31
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:32,930
Hello. Susan Stewart calling Mr. Levine, please.

32
00:01:32,930 --> 00:01:37,230
He's on the phone.

33
00:01:37,230 --> 00:01:40,550
Mr. Levine, Susan Stewart.

34
00:01:40,550 --> 00:01:43,850
I find myself in an embarrassing situation.

35
00:01:43,850 --> 00:01:46,010
I made another lunch date for today

36
00:01:46,010 --> 00:01:49,340
and forgot to enter it in my appointment book.

37
00:01:49,340 --> 00:01:52,530
Can you and I meet for drinks tomorrow?

38
00:01:52,530 --> 00:01:57,400
I'd really appreciate it.... Yes.... Thank you....

39
00:01:57,400 --> 00:02:00,060
Tomorrow at five o'clock at the Biltmore.

40
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:01,130
I'll see you then.

41
00:02:01,130 --> 00:02:27,660
Thank you, Mr. Levine.

42
00:02:27,660 --> 00:02:29,360
Welcome to the South Street restaurant, folks.

43
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,240
What'll it be?

44
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:31,380
What do you recommend?

45
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:33,360
Well, the crab salad's always a big hit.

46
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,830
Susan, would you like the crab salad?

47
00:02:34,830 --> 00:02:36,740
I'd love the crab salad.

48
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:38,800
Michelle, would you like to try the crab salad, too?

49
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:40,160
OK, Daddy.

50
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,000
We'll have three crab salads

51
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,930
and a pitcher of lemonade.

52
00:02:43,930 --> 00:02:48,150
Help yourself to celery and carrots and other vegetables.

53
00:02:48,150 --> 00:02:49,740
We used to catch crabs.

54
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:50,990
Where was that?

55
00:02:50,990 --> 00:02:53,040
We had a summer house on Fire Island.

56
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,350
Do you remember, Michelle?

57
00:02:54,350 --> 00:02:54,900
Sure.

58
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:57,260
You and Mommy used to take me on the ferryboat.

59
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:58,790
Sometimes, at night,

60
00:02:58,790 --> 00:03:01,080
we would go down to the beach and catch crabs,

61
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:02,410
remember?

62
00:03:02,410 --> 00:03:04,340
With a piece of meat on a string!

63
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:05,260
Right.

64
00:03:05,260 --> 00:03:21,260
Well, I think I'm going to go get us all some vegetables.

65
00:03:21,260 --> 00:03:22,820
There you go.

66
00:03:22,820 --> 00:03:30,930
Thank you.

67
00:03:30,930 --> 00:03:34,010
And some ice-cold lemonade.

68
00:03:34,010 --> 00:03:34,690
Thank you.

69
00:03:34,690 --> 00:03:40,600
Enjoy it.

70
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:43,570
Michelle, can I help you with the lemonade?

71
00:03:43,570 --> 00:03:44,240
No, thank you.

72
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:48,770
I'll wait for my father.

73
00:03:48,770 --> 00:03:50,910
Michelle, can we have a talk?

74
00:03:50,910 --> 00:03:52,870
Sure.

75
00:03:52,870 --> 00:03:54,620
I know you miss your mother.

76
00:03:54,620 --> 00:03:55,780
You do?

77
00:03:55,780 --> 00:03:59,790
Yes. And I'm not trying to take her place.

78
00:03:59,790 --> 00:04:01,570
Then why are you and Daddy

79
00:04:01,570 --> 00:04:03,890
spending so much time together?

80
00:04:03,890 --> 00:04:06,020
Because we like each other.

81
00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:09,180
And right now, he needs a friend.

82
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:10,390
I'm his friend.

83
00:04:10,390 --> 00:04:13,720
I know you are.

84
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:16,710
Sometimes he's very sad.

85
00:04:16,710 --> 00:04:18,900
And so are you, I think.

86
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:21,320
Sometimes.

87
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:25,300
I'd like to be your friend, too.

88
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:33,460
Will you let me be your friend, Michelle?

89
00:04:33,460 --> 00:04:36,900
So, what were you two talking about?

90
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:38,530
Just girl talk, Daddy.

91
00:04:38,530 --> 00:04:40,540
It's too hard to explain.

92
00:04:40,540 --> 00:04:41,530
You're probably right.

93
00:04:41,530 --> 00:04:44,530
Well, let's get started.
